CoMind Proprietary Rights Reservation
Version 1.0 | Prepared November 2, 2026

All rights in protectable CoMind-owned material are reserved by the respective
rights holders. This notice grants no general license to use, reproduce, modify,
distribute, sublicense, sell, or operate that material as a hosted service.
Permission must come from a rights holder with authority over the material in
question, through a separate written authorization identifying its scope.

Public availability is not an open-source license. GitHub platform permissions,
rights previously validly granted, third-party licenses, and rights or exceptions
provided by applicable law remain unaffected. This notice does not purport to
revoke those rights or to restrict material outside the rights holders' control.

No trademark, patent, endorsement, or ownership-transfer permission is granted
by this notice. No exclusive right in ideas, methods, public-domain material,
or unprotectable AI-generated expression is asserted by this notice.

Third-party components and adapted material retain their respective licenses
and notices. See docs/legal/THIRD-PARTY-RIGHTS.md. A separate license applicable
to a component controls that component; this notice does not relicense it.

The controlled-access agreement in docs/legal/CONTROLLED-ACCESS-AGREEMENT.md
is a review draft, not an executed agreement or a grant to repository visitors.
Repository access, a fork, or a contribution alone does not establish assent
to that agreement. Licensing requests may be directed to the repository
maintainer jlhogarth through GitHub; do not disclose confidential information
in public issues. Maintainer status alone does not establish chain of title.

See docs/legal/README.md for scope, review status, and activation requirements.
